hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1524","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd al-Muharibi al-Kufi narrated to us, saying:** Sharik narrated to us, from Abu al-Hasna', from al-Hakam, from Hanish, from 'Ali رضي الله عنه, that he used to offer two rams as a sacrifice (udhiyah): one on behalf of the Prophet ﷺ and the other on behalf of himself. When he was asked about this, he said: **\"He commanded me to do so\"** — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — **\"and I shall never abandon it.\"**\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: **\"This is a gharib (uncommon) Hadith. We do not know it except through the narration of Sharik.\"**\n\nHe further stated: **\"Some of the people of knowledge have permitted that a sacrifice be offered on behalf of the deceased, while others have held that no sacrifice should be offered on their behalf.\"**\n\n'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak said: **\"It is more beloved to me that charity be given on behalf of the deceased rather than a sacrifice be offered for them. However, if one does sacrifice, they should not eat anything from it and should give all of it in charity.\"**\n\nMuhammad (al-Bukhari) said: 'Ali ibn al-Madini said: **\"This Hadith has also been narrated by narrators other than Sharik.\"**\n\nI asked him: **\"What is the name of Abu al-Hasna'?\"** He did not know it. Muslim said: **\"His name is al-Hasan.\"**\n\n---\n\n*This narration is recorded in Sunan al-Tirmidhi and pertains to the permissibility of offering a sacrificial animal on behalf of the Prophet ﷺ after his passing, a matter upon which the scholars have differed.*"
"1525","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:\"I attended the Eid Al-Adha' with the Prophet (ﷺ) at the Musalla. When he finished his Khutbah"
"1526","Narrated by al-Bara' ibn 'Azib (may Allah be pleased with him), who reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\"One should not sacrifice a lame animal whose lameness is apparent, nor a one-eyed animal whose blindness is obvious, nor a sick animal whose illness is evident, nor an emaciated animal that has no marrow in its bones.\""
"1527","he should be given a name, and his head should be shaved. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1522 Arabic Hadees: 1522\""
"1528","Narrated Umm Salamah:That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever sees the crescent of Dhul-Hijjah"
"1529","Narrated 'Aishah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"There is no vowing for disobedience"
"1530","Narrated 'Aishah:That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"There is no vowing in disobedience to Allah"
"1531","Narrated Thabit bin Adh-Dahhak:That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"It is not for a person to vow about that over which he has no control"
"1532","Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"The atonement of a vow when it is not specified is the atonement of an oath"
"1533","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"O 'Abdur-Rahman! Do not ask for a position of leadership"
"1534","Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever takes an oath"
"1535","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever swears about an oath and says: 'If Allah wills (Insha Allah)"
"1536","Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever swears [about an oath] and says: 'If Allah wills (Insha Allah)"
"1537","Narrated Salim:From his father (Ibn 'Umar) that the Prophet (ﷺ) heard 'Umar saying: \"By my father"
"1538","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came across 'Umar while he was on his mount"
"1539","Narrated Sa'd bin 'Ubaidah:That Ibn 'Umar heard a man saying: \"No by the Ka'bah\" so Ibn 'Umar said: \"Nothing is sworn by other than Allah"
"1540","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Narrated by al-Bara' ibn 'Azib (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nHe said: \"The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) addressed us on the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Nahr) and said: **'None of you should slaughter until he has prayed.'**\n\nSo my maternal uncle stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this is a day in which meat is scarce (or undesirable), and I hastened my sacrifice so as to feed my family, the people of my household, or my neighbours.'\n\nHe (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **'Then repeat your slaughter (i.e., offer another sacrifice).'**\n\nHe said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have a young she-goat that is still nursing, and it is better than two sheep of meat. May I slaughter it?'\n\nHe (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **'Yes, and it is the best of your two sacrifices. And no *jadha'ah* (a young animal) shall suffice for anyone after you.'**\n\n---\n\n**Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said:** In this chapter (bab), there are narrations from Jabir, Jundab, Anas, 'Uwaymir ibn Ashqar, Ibn 'Umar, and Abu Zayd al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with them all).\n\n**Abu 'Isa said:** This is a *hasan sahih* hadith.\n\nThe practice (al-'amal) according to the majority of the scholars of knowledge is that no one should offer the sacrifice (*udhiyah*) in a city until the Imam has prayed. However, a group of scholars permitted the people of the villages to slaughter once dawn (fajr) has risen, and this is the view of Ibn al-Mubarak (may Allah have mercy on him).\n\n**Abu 'Isa said:** The scholars have unanimously agreed (*ajma'a*) that a *jadha'ah* from among goats (*al-ma'z*) does not suffice, and they stated that a *jadha'ah* suffices only from among sheep (*al-da'n*)."
"1541","Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Do not vow"
"1542","Narrated 'Umar:\"I said:'O Messenger of Allah! I had vowed to perform I'tikaf in Al-Masjid Al-Haram for a night during the era of Jahiliyyah.' He said: 'Fulfill your vow"
"1543","Narrated Salim bin 'Abdullah:From this father (Ibn Umar) who said: \"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) often would swear with this oath: 'No! By the Changer of the Hearts"
"1544","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\"I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Whoever frees a believing slave"
"1545","Narrated Suwaid bin Muqarrin Al-Muzani:\"We were seven brothers without a servant except one"
"1546","Narrated Thabit bin Adh-Dahhak:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam while lying"
"1547","Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir:\"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! My sister vowed that she would walk to the House barefoot and without Khimar (covering).' The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Verily Allah will not do anything with the misery of your sister. She should ride"
